{
  "id": "python",
  "displayName": "Python",
  "description": "Python interpreter with pip and venv (the python.org NuGet distribution).",
  "defaultVersion": "3.14.7",
  "versionCommand": {
    "executable": "python.exe",
    "args": [
      "--version"
    ],
    "outputPrefix": "Python "
  },
  "binDirs": [
    ".",
    "Scripts"
  ],
  "verifyFiles": [
    "python.exe",
    "Lib/site-packages/pip/__init__.py"
  ],
  "env": {
    "PYTHONNOUSERSITE": "1"
  },
  "shims": [
    {
      "name": "pip",
      "target": "python.exe",
      "args": [
        "-m",
        "pip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "pip3",
      "target": "python.exe",
      "args": [
        "-m",
        "pip"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "features": [
    {
      "id": "pip",
      "label": "pip (relocatable launcher)",
      "verifyFile": "Lib/site-packages/pip/__init__.py",
      "missingNote": "pip isn't in this install. Use Repair to reinstall it."
    },
    {
      "id": "venv",
      "label": "venv",
      "verifyFile": "Lib/venv/__init__.py",
      "missingNote": "This install has no venv module."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "python.org's NuGet package: full standard library with venv and pip (the embeddable ZIP has no pip). `pip` and `pip3` are small launchers OpenMind Studio writes next to the runtime; they find Python relative to themselves, so they keep working if you move the whole OpenMind Studio folder. Packages you install stay inside this install, and the system Python's user packages are hidden from it (PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1). Command launchers that pip itself creates for other packages (for example `black.exe`) record absolute paths and stop working after a move; run them as `python -m <name>`. tkinter/IDLE aren't included. python.org publishes no SHA256 for these packages, so each hash was computed from the official download when the version was pinned.",
